/**
\fn Attributes pdg::Attributes::withAppearance(Attributes overrides, boolean textOnly)
\brief Copy this drawing style with explicitly assigned appearance overrides.

\param overrides An Attributes or AnimatedAttributes sample. Only channels explicitly
set or scheduled on that source override this base. Setting a default value is explicit;
for example, roundedCorners(0) removes a base style's rounded corners.
\param textOnly Defaults to false. True applies only text size, text style, font,
fill opacity and blend mode, preserving the base foreground and other styling.
\return An independent Attributes snapshot. Neither source changes, and this base's
transform is preserved. Transform, location and size from overrides are not copied.

Appearance animation owns its channel when scheduled and contributes its current value;
this method does not advance either source. MVC uses this to compose View appearance
with the selected ControlAttributes state. Custom draw routines can use the same method.
\note API stability: 2 — Evolving.
*/
